{"stem": "peak-limiter", "name": "peak_limiter", "description": "Peak Limiter\n\nBrick-wall feed-forward peak limiter.  Detects the peak amplitude of each\naudio block and computes a gain factor to ensure the output never exceeds\nthe configured threshold.\n\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510    crag.peak    \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510   gain   \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510   crag.scale\n\u2502  input  \u2502 \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba \u2502 envelope \u2502 \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba \u2502 min(1, T/E\u2502 \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518                \u2502 follower \u2502           \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n\nSignal path:\n  1. Level detection:   crag.peak finds max|sample| in the current block.\n  2. Envelope follower: crag.smooth applies asymmetric 1-pole IIR at block rate.\n  3. Gain computation (linear domain \u2014 no log/exp on the envelope):\n       threshold_linear = exp(threshold_dB * ln(10)/20)\n       gain = min(1.0, threshold_linear / max(envelope, 1e-7))\n  4. Apply gain:   crag.scale multiplies every sample by the gain.\n\nBecause gain is derived from the CURRENT block's peak (zero look-ahead),\na short attack time (\u2248 1 ms) is recommended for hard transient protection.\nVery short attacks can introduce low-frequency intermodulation; increase\nattack time if audible distortion occurs on bass-heavy material.\n\nParameters:\n  threshold_db  [-24, 0]     dBFS limiting ceiling   (default  0 dB = unity)\n  attack_ms     [0.1, 50]    attack  time in ms       (default  1 ms)\n  release_ms    [10, 500]    release time in ms       (default 50 ms)\n\nUsage:\n  crag.include \"standard-graphs/compressors/peak-limiter.crag.mlir\" as \"peak_limiter\"\n\n  %limited = crag.subgraph_ref \"peak_limiter\"(%in)\n                 : (!crag.audio<f32, 48000, 1>) -> !crag.audio<f32, 0, 0>", "sr": 48000, "ch": 1, "build_meta": {"gen_datetime": "2026-07-03 23:12 UTC", "git_commit": "4f41407", "compiled_with": "f435c63"}, "wasm": "peak-limiter.wasm", "meta_file": "peak-limiter.wasm.cragmeta", "meta": {"schema_version": 1, "sample_rate": 48000, "channels": 1, "parameters": [{"name": "loop", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 1.0, "default": 1.0, "float_index": 0}, {"name": "threshold_db", "type": "float", "min": -24.0, "max": 0.0, "default": 0.0, "unit": "dB", "float_index": 1}, {"name": "attack_ms", "type": "float", "min": 0.1, "max": 50.0, "default": 1.0, "unit": "ms", "float_index": 2}, {"name": "release_ms", "type": "float", "min": 10.0, "max": 500.0, "default": 50.0, "unit": "ms", "float_index": 3}], "samplers": ["audio"], "texture_samplers": [], "events": [{"name": "start", "type": "void", "void_index": 0}, {"name": "stop", "type": "void", "void_index": 1}], "meters": [{"name": "progress", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 1.0, "float_index": 0}, {"name": "Output", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 1.0, "float_index": 1}], "has_visualizer": true, "has_audio_output": true, "viz_width": 512, "viz_height": 256, "compiled_with": "f435c63"}, "mca": {"graph": "peak-limiter", "block_size": 512, "results": [{"label": "Intel Haswell (x86-64-v3)", "triple": "x86_64-linux-gnu", "march": "x86-64", "mcpu": "haswell", "arch": "x86-64", "ipc": 1.25, "block_rthroughput": 75.25, "cycles_per_sample": 0.147, "insns_per_block": 184, "uops_per_block": 301}, {"label": "Intel Skylake-AVX512 (x86-64-v4)", "triple": "x86_64-linux-gnu", "march": "x86-64", "mcpu": "skylake-avx512", "arch": "x86-64", "ipc": 1.3976, "block_rthroughput": 50.17, "cycles_per_sample": 0.098, "insns_per_block": 186, "uops_per_block": 301}, {"label": "AMD Zen 3 (znver3)", "triple": "x86_64-l